{
    "id": "YOUR_MACHINE_IDENTITY_ENTITLEMENTS_SCAN_WORKFLOW_ID",
    "name": "Machine Identity Entitlements - Scan",
    "description": "Interactive scan of machine identities for entitlements to add from source accounts. Explains the process, runs custom:machine-identity-entitlements, then reports whether trigger accounts were written. The invoke body is a plain-text NDJSON stream, so every read of it is a string comparison, never a JSONPath into an object.",
    "definition": {
        "start": "Message About This Process",
        "steps": {
            "Message About This Process": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "INFO",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 22px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#0f172a;\">This process inspects <strong>machine identities</strong> and the entitlement values on their source accounts. It does not grant access itself. When an identity is missing catalog matches, a trigger account is written and <strong>Machine Identity Entitlements - Apply</strong> PATCHes <code>userEntitlements</code> as a union.</p><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0 14px;width:100%;max-width:660px;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#eff6ff;border-left:5px solid #2563eb;border-radius:6px;padding:20px 24px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#1d4ed8;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">1 &middot; What runs</div>Every machine identity in scope is evaluated. Machine accounts are read through their <code>machineIdentity</code> link. Each source selects the account field through <code>connectorAttributes.userEntitlements</code>. The default invoke scans every machine identity. Add <code>identityId</code> on the invoke step to limit to one.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"background-color:#f0fdf4;border-left:5px solid #16a34a;border-radius:6px;padding:20px 24px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#15803d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">2 &middot; What happens to a finding</div>A non-empty add list becomes one trigger account. Apply GETs the identity, then PATCHes existing <code>userEntitlements</code> plus the persisted ids. Empty add lists are not written, so Account Created does not fire.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fffbeb;border-left:5px solid #d97706;border-radius:6px;padding:20px 24px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b45309;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">3 &middot; While it runs</div>The scan is already running &mdash; this panel is information only and nothing is waiting on you. A large tenant takes several minutes. The outcome appears below this panel when it finishes.</td></tr></table>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Machine identity entitlements"
                },
                "description": "Explains the scan before any tenant API is called.",
                "displayName": "Message: About this process",
                "nextStep": "Configuration",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Configuration": {
                "actionId": "sp:define-variable",
                "attributes": {
                    "id": "sp:define-variable",
                    "variables": [
                        {
                            "description": "ISC API base URL, no trailing slash.",
                            "name": "API URL",
                            "transforms": [],
                            "variableA": "https://tenant.api.identitynow-demo.com"
                        },
                        {
                            "description": "Result source that stores custom operation output.",
                            "name": "SaaS Custom Operations Source Name",
                            "transforms": [],
                            "variableA": "SaaS Custom Operations"
                        },
                        {
                            "description": "Platform connector id for saas-custom-operations.",
                            "name": "SaaS Custom Operations Connector ID",
                            "transforms": [],
                            "variableA": "<CONNECTOR ID>"
                        }
                    ]
                },
                "displayName": "Configuration",
                "nextStep": "Get Access Token",
                "type": "Mutation"
            },
            "Get Access Token": {
                "actionId": "sp:http",
                "attributes": {
                    "formRequestBody": {
                        "grant_type": "client_credentials"
                    },
                    "method": "post",
                    "param_authenticationRef": "basic",
                    "param_basic": {
                        "mapping": {
                            "auth_password": "password",
                            "auth_username": "username"
                        },
                        "paramID": "YOUR_OAUTH_BASIC_AUTH_PARAM_ID",
                        "paramType": "1.1",
                        "refID": "YOUR_OAUTH_BASIC_AUTH_REF_ID"
                    },
                    "requestContentType": "form",
                    "url": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}/oauth/token"
                },
                "catch": [
                    {
                        "next": "Message Token Failed"
                    }
                ],
                "displayName": "Get Access Token",
                "nextStep": "Call SaaS Custom Operation",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 3
            },
            "Call SaaS Custom Operation": {
                "actionId": "sp:http",
                "attributes": {
                    "jsonRequestBody": {
                        "config": {
                            "apiUrl": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}",
                            "sourceName": "{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsSourceName}}",
                            "token": "{{$.getAccessToken.body.access_token}}"
                        },
                        "connectorRef": "{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsConnectorID}}",
                        "input": {
                            "requestId": "mie:{{$.trigger.interactiveProcessId}}"
                        },
                        "tag": "latest",
                        "type": "custom:machine-identity-entitlements"
                    },
                    "method": "post",
                    "param_authenticationRef": "none",
                    "param_basic": {
                        "mapping": {
                            "auth_password": "password",
                            "auth_username": "username"
                        },
                        "paramType": "1.1"
                    },
                    "requestContentType": "json",
                    "requestHeaders": {
                        "Authorization": "Bearer {{$.getAccessToken.body.access_token}}"
                    },
                    "url": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}/beta/platform-connectors/{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsConnectorID}}/invoke",
                    "urlParams": {}
                },
                "catch": [
                    {
                        "next": "Message Invoke Error"
                    }
                ],
                "description": "{{$.configuration.aPIURL}}/beta/platform-connectors/{{$.configuration.saaSCustomOperationsConnectorID}}/invoke",
                "displayName": "Call SaaS Custom Operation",
                "nextStep": "Check Invoke Result",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 3
            },
            "Check Invoke Result": {
                "actionId": "sp:compare-strings",
                "choiceList": [
                    {
                        "comparator": "StringContains",
                        "nextStep": "Message Scan Failed",
                        "variableA.$": "$.callSaaSCustomOperation.body",
                        "variableB": "\"status\":\"failed\""
                    }
                ],
                "defaultStep": "Check Trigger Accounts Written",
                "description": "The connector answers HTTP 200 even when the operation failed, so catch never fires for an operation-level failure. The body is a text/plain NDJSON stream, which is why this is a string check and not a JSONPath read.",
                "displayName": "Invoke failed?",
                "type": "choice"
            },
            "Check Trigger Accounts Written": {
                "actionId": "sp:compare-strings",
                "choiceList": [
                    {
                        "comparator": "StringContains",
                        "nextStep": "Message No Work",
                        "variableA.$": "$.callSaaSCustomOperation.body",
                        "variableB": "\"triggerAccountsWritten\":0"
                    }
                ],
                "defaultStep": "Message Work Written",
                "description": "triggerAccountsWritten is always present in the response summary, and the streamed JSON has no spaces after colons, so a zero result matches this literal exactly.",
                "displayName": "Any trigger accounts?",
                "type": "choice"
            },
            "Message No Work": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "INFO",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#f0fdf4;border-left:5px solid #16a34a;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#15803d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#14532d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">No entitlements to add</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">Every machine identity in scope already has its same-source catalog matches from configured machine-account connector attributes, or those accounts had nothing to match. No trigger account was written, so Apply will not run.</div></td></tr></table><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0 12px;width:100%;max-width:660px;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#eff6ff;border-left:5px solid #2563eb;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#1d4ed8;\">What this covers</strong> &mdash; machine identity <code>userEntitlements</code> from source-account values, not human identities or SoD.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border-left:5px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#475569;\">Scope</strong> &mdash; the default invoke scans every machine identity. Sources without <code>connectorAttributes.userEntitlements</code> are skipped.</td></tr></table>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan complete"
                },
                "description": "Zero trigger accounts. Empty add lists are not persisted, so Apply does not run.",
                "displayName": "Message: No work",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Success",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message Work Written": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "INFO",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#eff6ff;border-left:5px solid #2563eb;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#1d4ed8;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#1e3a8a;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Trigger accounts were written</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">The scan finished and persisted at least one add list. <strong>Machine Identity Entitlements - Apply</strong> runs on Account Created for each trigger account and unions those entitlement ids onto <code>userEntitlements</code>.</div></td></tr></table><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0 12px;width:100%;max-width:660px;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fffbeb;border-left:5px solid #d97706;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\"><strong style=\"color:#b45309;\">Apply must be enabled</strong> &mdash; if that workflow is disabled, the trigger accounts stay on the result source until it runs.</td></tr></table>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan complete"
                },
                "description": "At least one trigger account was written. Apply is expected to PATCH userEntitlements.",
                "displayName": "Message: Work written",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Success",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message Scan Failed": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "ERROR",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fef2f2;border-left:5px solid #dc2626;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b91c1c;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#7f1d1d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">The scan stopped before it finished</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">The connector answered, but the operation reported a failure. Trigger accounts from this run are incomplete, and no new entitlements were applied from this invoke.</div></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#64748b;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Operation response</div><div style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 20px;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;color:#334155;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;\">{{$.callSaaSCustomOperation.body}}</div>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan did not complete"
                },
                "description": "Operation-level failure. The body carries the error text, which is the only place the cause appears.",
                "displayName": "Message: Scan failed",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Failure",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message Invoke Error": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "ERROR",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fef2f2;border-left:5px solid #dc2626;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b91c1c;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#7f1d1d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">The connector could not be reached</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">The scan never started, so no trigger accounts were written and Apply will not run.</div></td></tr></table><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 24px 10px 0;vertical-align:top;width:150px;font-size:13px;color:#64748b;\">Status</td><td style=\"padding:10px 0;vertical-align:top;font-size:14px;color:#0f172a;\"><strong>{{$.callSaaSCustomOperation.error.workflowStatusCode}}</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 24px 10px 0;vertical-align:top;width:150px;font-size:13px;color:#64748b;\">Detail</td><td style=\"padding:10px 0;vertical-align:top;font-size:14px;color:#0f172a;\">{{$.callSaaSCustomOperation.error.workflowErrorMessage}}</td></tr></table><div style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border-left:5px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">Check the connector id and API URL in Configuration, and confirm the connector version is deployed to this tenant.</div>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan could not start"
                },
                "description": "Transport-level failure on the invoke, where the error object exists and the body does not.",
                "displayName": "Message: Invoke error",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Failure",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "Message Token Failed": {
                "actionId": "sp:interactive-message",
                "attributes": {
                    "category": "ERROR",
                    "interactiveProcessId.$": "$.trigger.interactiveProcessId",
                    "message": "<table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"background-color:#fef2f2;border-left:5px solid #dc2626;border-radius:6px;padding:24px 26px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#b91c1c;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Result</div><div style=\"font-size:20px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;color:#7f1d1d;margin:0 0 10px 0;\">Could not authenticate to the tenant</div><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">The OAuth token request failed, so the scan never ran.</div></td></tr></table><table role=\"presentation\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px 0;\"><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 24px 10px 0;vertical-align:top;width:150px;font-size:13px;color:#64748b;\">Status</td><td style=\"padding:10px 0;vertical-align:top;font-size:14px;color:#0f172a;\"><strong>{{$.getAccessToken.error.workflowStatusCode}}</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:10px 24px 10px 0;vertical-align:top;width:150px;font-size:13px;color:#64748b;\">Detail</td><td style=\"padding:10px 0;vertical-align:top;font-size:14px;color:#0f172a;\">{{$.getAccessToken.error.workflowErrorMessage}}</td></tr></table><div style=\"background-color:#f8fafc;border-left:5px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:6px;padding:18px 22px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:#1e293b;\">Re-apply the basic-auth reference on <strong>Get Access Token</strong> after import, and confirm the client id and secret are valid for this tenant.</div>",
                    "ownerId.$": "$.trigger.launchedBy.id",
                    "title": "Scan could not start"
                },
                "description": "OAuth failure. The basic-auth reference is tenant-specific and does not survive an import.",
                "displayName": "Message: Token failed",
                "nextStep": "End Step - Failure",
                "type": "action",
                "versionNumber": 1
            },
            "End Step - Success": {
                "actionId": "sp:operator-success",
                "displayName": "Success: Scan complete",
                "type": "success"
            },
            "End Step - Failure": {
                "actionId": "sp:operator-failure",
                "displayName": "Failure: Scan did not complete",
                "failureName": "Machine Identity Entitlements Scan Failed",
                "type": "failure"
            }
        }
    },
    "enabled": false,
    "trigger": {
        "type": "EVENT",
        "attributes": {
            "filter.$": "$[?(@.workflowId == 'YOUR_MACHINE_IDENTITY_ENTITLEMENTS_SCAN_WORKFLOW_ID')]",
            "id": "idn:interactive-process-launched",
            "integrationId": null
        }
    }
}
